    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stephens City was founded on October 12, 1758 by Peter Stephens, becoming the second oldest town in the Shenandoah Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephens_City%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town evolved through names—Stephensburg, Newtown, and finally Stephens City—though it almost became Pantops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephens_City%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1867 the Winchester and Strasburg Railroad linked Stephens City to the nation, boosting the local economy but ending the wagon‑building trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephens_City%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic center surveys identified key buildings, and their renovation has drawn heritage tourists to Stephens City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
